        "text": "mergeGate allows skipped required jobs to pass",
        "line": 288,
        "evidence": {
          "quote": "    const passed = spec.required.every((key) =>\n      jobs.some((job) => job.key === key && job.status === \"completed\" && (job.conclusion === \"success\" || job.conclusion === \"skipped\")),\n    );",
          "why": "docs/10 Project CI.md states under Merge gate: \"Merge gate: a native merge needs the newest run for the exact head SHA and the current revision, with every required job success.\" Skipped is a job conclusion defined separately from success; skipped jobs are produced when a need fails. Treating skipped as success lets a required job satisfy the gate even though it did not run successfully (e.g., its dependency failed), which violates the spec and could merge broken code."
        }
      }
